meta {
  name: Lookup product by GTIN
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/products/gtin/{{gtin}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    bru.setEnvVar("productId", res.getBody().id);
  }
}

docs {
  TICKET-P6-009 — the only way to resolve a GTIN to a product. On a local cache miss the server
  falls back to Open Food Facts and creates the Product + PackagedProduct rows in one transaction.

  Response shape: { id, kind, name, brand, image, description, status, unverified,
  submittedByUserId?, packaged: { gtin, genericName, ...nutrition, ingredients } | null, submission? }.

  - All products include unverified: boolean.
  - VERIFIED products: unverified: false.
  - PENDING_REVIEW products: unverified: true, plus a flat submission object, and submittedByUserId
    for registered callers.

  Visibility (P5-007, via services/productVisibility.ts):
  - PENDING_REVIEW products are returned to every caller. The anonymous copy omits submittedByUserId.
  - REJECTED products return 404 for every caller.
  - Voting stays registered-only: POST/DELETE /products/:productId/verify answer an anonymous token with 403.

  On success the post-response script stores `productId` for every chained request below (Get product
  by id, Approve/Reject, Correct, Propose edit, Get pending edit, Create/update rating, Get ratings).

  Errors: 400 (invalid GTIN format), 404 (not found / REJECTED).
}
